section: ghci
synopsis: Fix breakpoints in threads forked from the evaluated expression
issues: #28124
mrs: !16991

description: {
  Previously, breakpoints hit by threads forked from an evaluated expression
  could be silently ignored or reported (and resumed) from another evaluation.

  The breakpoint action is now installed once and never changed. Each thread
  that hits a breakpoint is resumed and reports its status independently.
  This makes debugging multi-threaded programs no longer unsound and it paves
  the way forward for a debugger with fine-grained control over what threads
  are paused and resumed.

  In particular, the following was fixed:
  - When an expression forks several threads that all hit a breakpoint,
    every breakpoint is now reported, rather than only the first.
  - Evaluating an expression while stopped (e.g. ``:force``) no longer
    consumes or discards breakpoints hit by threads of another evaluation;
    they are reported on the next ``:continue``.
  - ``^C`` during ``:continue`` of a forked thread now interrupts that thread
    with the external interpreter too.
}
